  "remark_ssdtHPET": "Resolves IRQ conflicts, typically used for audio fixes",
  "note_ssdtHPET": "• Fixes IRQ conflicts by patching legacy IRQs\n• Often needed for on-board audio to work properly\n• Only select if recommended or if facing audio issues",
  "remark_ssdtECUSBXDesktop": "Spoofs EC and injects USB power properties (Intel 6th Gen+ Desktop)",
  "note_ssdtECUSBXDesktop": "• Spoofs EC to allow macOS power management to load\n• Injects USB power properties for correct USB power delivery\n• Suitable for Intel Skylake (6th Gen) and newer desktop platforms",
  "remark_ssdtECUSBXLaptop": "Spoofs EC, does not affect existing EC, injects USB power properties (Intel 6th Gen+ Laptop)",
  "note_ssdtECUSBXLaptop": "• Spoofs EC (Embedded Controller) without affecting the existing one\n• Injects USB power properties for laptops\n• Suitable for Intel Skylake (6th Gen) and newer laptop platforms",
  "remark_ssdtECDesktop": "Spoofs EC (Intel 5th Gen and older Desktop)",
  "note_ssdtECDesktop": "• Spoofs EC to allow macOS power management to load\n• Suitable for Intel Broadwell (5th Gen) and older desktop platforms",
  "remark_ssdtECLaptop": "Spoofs EC, does not affect existing EC (Intel 5th Gen and older Laptop)",
  "note_ssdtECLaptop": "• Spoofs EC (Embedded Controller) without affecting the existing one\n• Suitable for Intel Broadwell (5th Gen) and older laptop platforms",
  "remark_ssdtUSBX": "USB power properties fix (Intel 6th Gen+)",
  "note_ssdtUSBX": "• Injects USB power properties for correct USB power delivery\n• Suitable for Intel Skylake (6th Gen) and newer platforms",
  "remark_ssdtPLUG": "CPU core recognition, enables frequency scaling and power saving",
  "note_ssdtPLUG": "• Injects plugin-type=1 on the first processor\n• Enables native macOS CPU power management and frequency scaling\n• Required on Intel Haswell (4th Gen) to Comet Lake (10th Gen)",
  "remark_ssdtPMC": "Enables NVRAM support (Typically Intel 300 series native motherboards)",
  "note_ssdtPMC": "• Adds missing PMC device for native NVRAM support\n• Required on Intel 300 series motherboards (Z390, B360, etc.)",
  "remark_ssdtPNLF": "Adds PNLF device for backlight support (Laptops and AIOs)",
  "note_ssdtPNLF": "• Injects PNLF device required for macOS backlight control\n• Essential for Laptops and All-in-One devices",
  "remark_ssdtALS0": "Provides ambient light sensor support (Laptops and AIOs)",
  "note_ssdtALS0": "• Spoofs an ambient light sensor (ALS0)\n• Helps with screen brightness persistence and auto-brightness on laptops",
  "remark_ssdtXOSI": "macOS spoofs Windows, unlocks hidden devices (e.g., I2C trackpad)",
  "note_ssdtXOSI": "• Spoofs Windows version during ACPI OS check\n• Unlocks devices hidden by the BIOS (like I2C trackpads)\n• Requires _OSI to XOSI rename patch",
  "remark_ssdtRHUB": "USB port reset and fix",
  "note_ssdtRHUB": "• Disables the original RHUB device and forces macOS to enumerate USB ports again\n• Useful for Asus motherboards on 400-series chipsets",
  "remark_ssdtBridge": "Creates bridges for missing PCI device paths",
  "note_ssdtBridge": "• Adds missing PCI bridges to the ACPI tree\n• Ensures devices are mounted correctly in macOS",
  "remark_ssdtDMAR": "Removes DMAR reserved memory region, fixes system boot and network issues",
  "note_ssdtDMAR": "• Drops original DMAR table and replaces it without the reserved memory region\n• Fixes issues with Intel I225-V Ethernet and certain Wi-Fi cards",
  "remark_ssdtAPIC": "Adds missing APIC entries for more than 255 threads",
  "note_ssdtAPIC": "• Required on systems with more than 255 threads to boot macOS",
  "remark_ssdtSBUSMCHC": "Adds SMBus support",
  "note_ssdtSBUSMCHC": "• Completes the ACPI tree for SMBus (System Management Bus)\n• Enables AppleSMBus and fixes temperature sensors",
  "remark_ssdtIMEI": "Fixes iGPU acceleration failure (Typically Ivy Bridge and Sandy Bridge)",
  "note_ssdtIMEI": "• Adds or fixes the IMEI (Intel Management Engine Interface) device\n• Required for Intel HD 3000/4000 graphics acceleration",
  "remark_ssdtFixShutdown": "Fixes restart after shutdown or shutdown failure",
  "note_ssdtFixShutdown": "• Fixes the issue where the PC restarts instead of shutting down\n• Usually requires an ACPI rename patch (_PTS to ZPTS)",
  "remark_checkSystemState": "Check System State",
  "note_checkSystemState": "• Verifies system ACPI state for compatibility",
  "remark_checkAOAC": "Check AOAC",
  "note_checkAOAC": "• Checks Always-On Always-Connected compatibility",
  "remark_ssdtGPRW": "Fixes instant wake caused by USB controllers",
  "note_ssdtGPRW": "• Prevents USB devices from instantly waking the system from sleep\n• Requires GPRW to XPRW rename patch",
  "remark_ssdtUPRW": "Fixes instant wake caused by USB controllers",
  "note_ssdtUPRW": "• Alternative to GPRW patch to prevent instant wake",
  "remark_ssdtLID": "Fixes laptop lid sleep/wake issues",
  "note_ssdtLID": "• Ensures the system correctly enters sleep when the lid is closed and wakes when opened",
  "remark_ssdtWakeScreen": "Fixes screen not waking up after sleep",
  "note_ssdtWakeScreen": "• Injects a power button press to wake the screen",
  "remark_ssdtLED": "Fixes laptop LED status indicators after wake",
  "note_ssdtLED": "• Fixes breathing light and power button LED on Lenovo laptops after wake",
  "remark_ssdtS3Disable": "Disables S3 sleep state (Fixes crash, reboot or shutdown on wake)",
  "note_ssdtS3Disable": "• Disables macOS S3 sleep state to prevent crashes on wake\n• Requires _S3 to XS3 rename patch",
  "remark_ssdtFACP": "Changes warm reboot to cold reboot, fixes disabled hardware",
  "note_ssdtFACP": "• Changes warm reboot to cold reboot\n• Fixes issues where Wi-Fi, Bluetooth or Audio are disabled after rebooting from Windows to macOS",
  "remark_ssdtGPUSPOOF": "Spoofs GPU",
  "note_ssdtGPUSPOOF": "• Modifies device ID for unsupported AMD GPUs (like RX 550 Lexa, RX 6650XT) to a supported model to enable acceleration",
  "remark_ssdtPCIDISABLE": "Disables PCI devices (unsupported GPUs, NVMe SSDs, etc.)",
  "note_ssdtPCIDISABLE": "• Disables unsupported PCIe devices like discrete GPUs or specific NVMe drives via ACPI",
  "remark_ssdtRMNE": "Spoofs Ethernet device (For laptops without Ethernet)",
  "note_ssdtRMNE": "• Injects a NullEthernet device (en0)\n• Required for Apple services (iMessage, Facetime, iCloud) on laptops without an Ethernet port",
  "remark_ssdtGPI0": "Fixes I2C trackpad issues (Laptops)",
  "note_ssdtGPI0": "• Enables the GPI0 device in ACPI for macOS\n• Required for many I2C trackpads to function correctly",
  "remark_ssdtCPUR": "CPU rename for B850, B650, B550, A520 chipsets (Ryzen only)",
  "note_ssdtCPUR": "• Renames AMD CPU in ACPI to fix boot crashes on newer AMD chipsets",
  "remark_ssdtPLUGALT": "Power management fix (Intel 12th Gen+ and some AMD Ryzen)",
  "note_ssdtPLUGALT": "• Injects plugin-type=1 on newer processors\n• Required for macOS CPU power management on Intel Alder Lake and newer, and some AMD platforms",
  "remark_ssdtAWAC": "Disables AWAC (Modern Timer) (Intel 8th Gen+)",
  "note_ssdtAWAC": "• Disables the modern AWAC timer and enables the legacy RTC\n• Required on Intel Coffee Lake (8th Gen) and newer",
  "remark_ssdtUNC": "Required for native X99 (C612) and most X79 (C602) motherboards",
  "note_ssdtUNC": "• Disables unused devices in ACPI to prevent IOPCIFamily kernel panics on X99/X79 boards",
  "remark_ssdtRTC0RANGE": "Enables/spoofs legacy RTC timer and fixes RTC range (X99 and X299)",
  "note_ssdtRTC0RANGE": "• Enables legacy RTC timer and fixes RTC range errors on X99 and X299 boards",
  "remark_ssdtDTGP": "Adds DTGP support",
  "note_ssdtDTGP": "• Injects hardware properties for GPUs, audio, Thunderbolt cards",
  "remark_ssdtDMAC": "Spoofs a standard DMA controller",
  "note_ssdtDMAC": "• Spoofs a standard DMA Controller (PNP0200)\n• Completes ACPI resource table for LPC bus and DMA",
  "remark_ssdtPWRB": "Spoofs a standard PWRB controller",
  "note_ssdtPWRB": "• Spoofs a Power Button (PNP0C0C) device\n• Ensures macOS correctly identifies the power button for sleep/wake",
  "remark_ssdtSLPB": "Spoofs a standard SLPB controller",
  "note_ssdtSLPB": "• Spoofs a Sleep Button (PNP0C0E) device\n• Ensures macOS correctly identifies the sleep button",
  "remark_ssdtMEM2": "Spoofs MEM2 device required for iGPU",
  "note_ssdtMEM2": "• Adds MEM2 ACPI device required for Intel integrated graphics on Haswell to Kaby Lake",
